From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.18 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-phy: reach PHY package data through phy_package accessors

6.18 moved struct phy_package_shared out of include/linux/phy.h into
drivers/net/phy/phy_package.c as a private type; the public header only
keeps the pointer in struct phy_device (phydev->shared).  qca-nss-phy
still declares the struct and reads its members directly:

  linux_std/qce1204/qce1204.c, qce1204_hwmon.c, qcom_phy_lib.c,
  linux_std/qca8084/qca8084.c, linux_std/ptp/qca808x_phc.c,
  linux_std/macsec/qca_macsec_lib.c, nss_ext/nss_phy_linux_wrapper.c

which fails with "invalid use of undefined type 'struct
phy_package_shared'" for every member access.  Also, 6.18 no longer
declares devm_of_phy_package_join() outside the private phylib.h, so
qce1204.c:2340 got an implicit declaration.

Replace the member reads with the exported accessors and drop the now
unusable local declarations; the NULL checks keep testing
phydev->shared, which remains a plain pointer:

  shared->priv       -> phy_package_get_priv(phydev)
  shared->np         -> phy_package_get_node(phydev)
  shared->base_addr  -> phy_package_get_base_addr(phydev)

phy_package_get_base_addr() does not exist upstream; kernel patch 0513
(25.12-6.18/patches/0029) adds it next to the other accessors, and also
restores the package-join prototypes in include/linux/phy.h so
out-of-tree PHY drivers see them.  Comments still mention the old member
names; they describe the concept and are left alone.

Classification: portability (kernel API, no behaviour change).
